     "Hi all,\r<br>   I am doing point transects for a single species of bird, Bachman&#39;s\r<br>Sparrow, to determine effects of growing season prescribed fire.\r<br>Sometimes I don&#39;t count any Sparrows at a point, consequently I have\r<br>zero birds for that point.  Since Distance makes it&#39;s calculations when\r<br>I input a distance, how do I input zero detections?  I guess my question\r<br>is really just a matter of syntax....how do I make sure that Distance\r<br>knows that I surveyed the point and found zero birds.  Please let me\r<br>know if this question needs clarification.\r<br>thanks,\r<br>clark jones\r<br>\r<br>--\r<br>distance-sampling list home page:\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792479227244000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0VTapHRJPQznFFS6VheAd6\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/lists/distance-sampling.html</a>\r<br>To unsubscribe, go to the home page and click &quot;Join or leave the list&quot;,\r<br>  or email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jisc...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a> with the following message body:\r<br>  leave distance-sampling\r<br>Before posting to the list, read the list guidelines at\r<br>  <a href=\"http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792479227244000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pzdccJxAcqTpO0lhBqOUX\">http://www.jiscmail.ac.uk/files/distance-sampling/</a>\r<br>    distance-sampling.welcome\r<br>Any questions, email the list owner at\r<br>  <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sam...@jiscmail.ac.uk</a>\r<br>--\r<br>"
